### Playground vs a real compiler

Everything in these lessons ran in the playground sandbox: network blocked, files under /tmp only and cleared between runs, processes contained, and the environment reduced to a whitelist. That is what keeps a shared playground safe, and it is why the reference panel badges some modules `limited` or `blocked`.

When you want the rest of the system - files that persist, the network, full process control - download the real compiler from xiom-lang.org. It is the same language and the same standard library, with no sandbox in the way.
